! C2H7O3Cl | PRE-OPTIMIZATION at wB97X-D/6-31G(d,p)/PCM(water)
!
! ============================================================
! Why this file exists
! ============================================================
! caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPPb/c/d all showed the same pathology: energy
! dropping far faster than the geometry was moving, and a growing negative
! Hessian curvature from the very first optimization step. TZVPPd (IHREP=2,
! forcing a genuinely fresh Hessian every 2 steps rather than one slowly
! propagated by BFGS) gave the decisive evidence: at NSERCH=2 and NSERCH=3,
! TWO INDEPENDENTLY COMPUTED Hessians each showed 15 SIMULTANEOUS NEGATIVE
! EIGENVALUES, closely matching each other in value. That rules out numerical
! noise (noise does not reproduce like that) and confirms this is a real
! feature of the wB97X-D/def2-TZVPP/PCM(water) surface at this geometry: it
! is not a stationary point of any kind, let alone a minimum.
!
! The source of the mismatch was then found directly: caa005bIRC.cml (the
! 290-point IRC this starting geometry was extracted from, at Reaction
! Coordinate step 1) was NOT computed at wB97X-D/def2-TZVPP. Its embedded
! basis set exponents (e.g. carbon 1S: 3047.52, 456.424, 103.653, 29.2258,
! 9.34863, 3.18904) match the classic Pople 6-31G(d) contraction, not
! def2-TZVPP -- and its reported energies (~-765.89) differ from ours
! (~-491.67) by ~274 Hartree, far too large to be a basis-quality effect
! alone, strongly suggesting a different method entirely generated this path.
! A geometry that is a good minimum on one PES has no reason to be anywhere
! near a stationary point on a different one -- 15 negative eigenvalues is
! entirely consistent with that, not evidence of a technical mistake.
!
! ============================================================
! What this file does
! ============================================================
! Standard practice for exactly this situation: relax the borrowed geometry
! at a CHEAPER level first, using the SAME functional and solvent treatment
! as the final target (wB97X-D, PCM water) but a smaller, GAMESS-NATIVE basis
! (6-31G(d,p) via GBASIS=N31 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 -- no custom BASNAM
! needed, so no risk of a transcription error in this bridging step). This
! should land within (or much closer to) the actual basin of attraction of a
! genuine minimum on the wB97X-D surface, before spending the much larger
! cost of the full def2-TZVPP basis.
!
! Optimizer settings carried over from the TZVPPd diagnosis (conservative
! DXMAX, frequent Hessian recomputation) since the SAME functional's lack of
! an analytic Hessian applies regardless of basis size. IHREP tightened to 1
! (recompute every step) since the smaller basis makes this much cheaper than
! it was for def2-TZVPP.
!
! Next step once this converges cleanly (Hessian free of large/multiple
! negative eigenvalues, i.e. an actual minimum): take the resulting relaxed
! geometry and re-run the full wB97X-D/def2-TZVPP/PCM(water) optimization
! (caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPPd's settings) starting from there instead of the
! raw IRC-extracted structure.

 $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE DFTTYP=wB97X-D
         COORD=UNIQUE MAXIT=200 NOSYM=1
 $END
 $GUESS GUESS=HUCKEL $END
 $BASIS GBASIS=N31 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 $END
 $SCF CONV=1.0D-6
     SOSCF=.T.
     DAMP=.F.
     SHIFT=.T.
     DIRSCF=.TRUE.
 $END
 $STATPT OPTTOL=0.0001 NSTEP=300 IHREP=1 HSSEND=.T. DXMAX=0.02 NPRT=1 $END
 $ZMAT DLC=.F. AUTO=.F. $END
 $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM PROJCT=.T. $END
 $PCM SOLVNT=WATER $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=100 MEMDDI=200 $END

 $DATA
Chloroacetaldehyde hydrate and water -- pre-relaxation at 6-31G(d,p)
C1
Cl   17.0   3.31777   0.19618   0.40668
C     6.0   2.24118   0.90662  -0.95961
C     6.0   3.04189   1.88482  -1.77661
O     8.0   2.47874   2.79975  -2.40567
H     1.0   1.37854   1.36717  -0.48364
H     1.0   1.95549   0.05691  -1.58084
O     8.0   3.58112   0.05498  -3.89961
O     8.0   3.79699   2.62132  -4.86879
H     1.0   3.58756   3.03704  -5.71005
H     1.0   3.65634   0.88740  -4.40943
H     1.0   2.96923  -0.51508  -4.37329
H     1.0   4.12539   1.74751  -1.81197
H     1.0   3.29383   3.07126  -4.16999
 $END
